    ('BUKD-P 525', 'PROJECT MANAGEMENT', '15060', 'Class Status', 'M Monday 7:30 PM–8:45 PM', 'WB WEB', 'Rex Cutshall', 5, NULL, 'Lecture', '3', 'WEB-BASED CLASS', ARRAY[]::TEXT[], 'This course is an introduction to project management. The course covers both predictive (traditional) and adaptive (agile) methodologies and when to use each. The course explores common reasons for project failure with a focus on the project triangle. Students will learn about charters, scheduling, scrums, and available certifications.', ARRAY['Kelley Direct Program Bloomington'], NULL),
