    ('EAS-E 144', 'EXTREME WEATHER AND ITS IMPACTS', '37483', 'Class Status', 'MW Monday, Wednesday 8:00 AM–10:30 AM', 'WB WEB', 'Chanh Kieu', 1, NULL, 'Lecture', '3', 'WEB-BASED CLASS', ARRAY[]::TEXT[], 'Introduces a range of natural disasters and extreme weather phenomena that span regions, seasons, and origins. Emphasizes the ingredients and causes of each phenomenon, as well as their physical and societal impacts. Types of disasters include floods, droughts and wildfires, thunderstorms and tornadoes, and hurricanes.', ARRAY['IUB GenEd N&M credit - Natural Science
