    ('PHIL-P 135', 'INTRODUCTION TO EXISTENTIALISM', '10091', 'Class Status', 'TuTh Tuesday, Thursday 1:55 PM–2:45 PM', 'BH 003', 'David Sussman', 10, 'Lecture', 'Lecture', '3', 'BALLANTINE HALL', ARRAY[]::TEXT[], 'Philosophical themes in nineteenth- and twentieth-century existentialism. Topics may include free choice and human responsibility, the nature of values, the influence of phenomenology on existentialism, and existentialism as illustrated in literature. Readings from some or all of: Buber, Camus, Heidegger, Husserl, Jaspers, Kierkegaard, Marcel, Nietzsche, Beauvoir, and Sartre. No prior knowledge of philosophy is presupposed.', ARRAY['IUB GenEd A&H credit
COLL (CASE) A&H Breadth of Inquiry credit'], NULL),
