    ('PSY-P 336', 'PSYCHOLOGICAL TESTS AND INDIVIDUAL DIFFERENCES', '29904', 'Closed', NULL, 'WB WEB', 'Joel Nadler', 0, NULL, 'Lecture', '3', 'WEB-BASED CLASS', ARRAY[]::TEXT[], 'Principles of psychological testing. Representative tests and their uses for evaluation and prediction. Emphasis on concepts of reliability, validity, standardization, norms, and item analysis.', ARRAY['COLL (CASE) N&M Breadth of Inquiry credit
